[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3622259147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113654#issuecomment-3622259147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113654","id":3622259147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X50nL","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-07T14:40:59Z","updated_at":"2025-12-07T14:40:59Z","body":"This PR will essentially turn every kinematic body into a static body, since you're setting both the \"from\" and \"to\" transforms to be the same value, meaning the linear/angular velocity of the body will always be zero and thus any collision response elicited by it will no longer be correct.\r\n\r\nI've put up another PR which instead changes kinematic bodies to always return `kinematic_transform` instead of its actual transform: #113712","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3622259147/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3623751235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113654#issuecomment-3623751235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113654","id":3623751235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X_g5D","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-07T23:23:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T10:33:37Z","body":"@mihe I see the issue now you are describing with this pr. Unfortunately, your pr does not help my use case with regards to the problem because I actually need the body to move in the physics server. I made an [mrp](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24020567/kinematic-area_overlap_2025-12-07_15-09-57.zip) to help show my specific problem. I want to move an area at the same time as a kinematic body and prevent it from leaving the area.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3623751235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627032492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113654#issuecomment-3627032492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113654","id":3627032492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YMB-s","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T13:48:15Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T13:48:15Z","body":"> I want to move an area at the same time as a kinematic body and prevent it from leaving the area.\r\n\r\nRight, yeah, that will indeed not be solved by #113712. The only real solution to that would be to introduce some new method that lets us actually distinguish between moving and \"teleporting\" a kinematic body.\r\n\r\nWe could perhaps take inspiration from the `Node.reset_physics_interpolation()` method (which sort of achieves the same thing) and have a method that \"resets\" the transform of a kinematic body to be the same as its desired/target transform (i.e. `kinematic_transform` in the Jolt implementation).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627032492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]